Tells GitHub Pages not to run the build output through Jekyll.

Without this, Jekyll strips every directory whose name begins with an
underscore — which on this site is `_nuxt/`, i.e. all of the JavaScript and CSS.
The page would load and then be entirely unstyled and inert.

The Actions deployment used here uploads an artifact rather than letting Pages
build the branch, so Jekyll should not run anyway. This file costs nothing and
removes the failure mode completely.
